# WN22-CC-000170: Windows Server 2022 network selection user interface (UI) must not be displayed on the logon screen.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000170-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 network selection user interface (UI) must not be displayed on the logon screen.`
    description `Enabling interaction with the network selection UI allows users to change connections to available networks without signing in to Windows.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:CM-7`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> System >> Logon >> Do not display network selection UI to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\System' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by setting registry value 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\System' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_7 `Windows Server implements CM-7 by setting registry value 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\System' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\System`
        name `DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
